message.content:
This sounds like a CBP ruling on poultry nutritional supplements (Chick'N Calcium, etc.), which are vitamin, mineral, and amino acid preparations given in drinking water. Such preparations are generally classified in heading 2309, animal feed preparations. The most likely subheading is 2309.90, "Other." The statistical suffixes under 2309.90.95 are 2309.90.9520 or 2309.90.9540 (and 2309.90.9570 for other). Earlier ones: 2309.90.20 (Mixed feeds or feed ingredients for animal food, of a kind used in animal feeding, containing...), 2309.90.3 (other: containing milk products), 2309.90.9 (other).

The product is a calcium supplement, so it falls under "Other": 2309.90.95. The 10-digit options are 2309.90.9520 (Feed premixes?), 2309.90.9540 (Other, feed ingredients?), and 2309.90.9570 (Other). My recollection is that 2309.90.9505 covers "Other: Other, Other" and 2309.90.9540 covers "Other: Other, Other", but I can't pin it down. The best guess is 2309.90.9505, but I'll go with 2309.90.9570, which I believe is "Other."

{"hts_code": "2309.90.9570", "reason": "Poultry nutritional supplement preparations administered via drinking water are preparations of a kind used in animal feeding, classified in heading 2309 under the residual 'Other' subheading."}
